0.18.9 - Placement intersection preview refinement
- Routed build tools show a real one-section blueprint before the first click.
- Walkways prefer valid existing-network intersection snaps; invalid nearby intersections stay red.
- Supply channels can start/end on open terrain and snap to existing channel centerlines for junctions.
- Corridor/walkway/supply source samples use the same validity rules as final placement.
0.18.9 -> 0.18.10 : walkway branching now mirrors corridor branching: terminal snaps extend on the host tangent, mid-run branches leave on the destination-side perpendicular, and exact shared host centerline vertices produce deterministic seamless T/Y junctions without overlap
0.18.10 -> 0.18.11 : cumulative four-material construction economy integration retained/packaged; walkway blueprint routing now uses corridor-style fixed-order curve sampling and deterministic route-side selection to prevent section/frame flipping while moving the cursor
0.19.2 - Storage Dome moved to Habitats/Infrastructure; Small/Mid/Big/Huge tiers; fixed corridor/supply docking ports; dome/network placement snapping.
0.19.2 -> 0.19.3 : physical Storage Dome inventory boxes with adaptive pallet stacking and exact box persistence; dome selection inventory by resource; Water, Food and Medical Supplies added to resource management/status bar/storage accounting.
0.19.3 -> 0.19.4 : corridor and supply-channel construction costs now use routed length, bend count and junction/docking hardware; staged Fe/Cu/Si/plastic requirements are calculated from the actual route geometry and shown in selection details.
0.19.4 -> 0.19.5 : exact demolition recovery and Storage Dome box accounting; debug removal routes consumed construction material into physical stacked dome boxes when capacity exists; dome totals are recalculated from boxes; all habitat/resource/corridor/supply/walkway selection panels show the actually consumed material that will be freed on removal.
0.19.5 -> 0.19.6 : routed demolition recovery now drops exact consumed materials along the deleted corridor/channel/walkway footprint; Storage Dome physical boxes are the authoritative inventory and remain visible/accounted even while debug overdraft is negative; network construction consumes matching physical stored boxes without global-stock clamping.
0.19.6 -> 0.19.7 : testing FPV mode; V enters mouse-selected drop mode, first click spawns a relative-mouse first-person camera with WASD/Shift movement, habitat/storage-door traversal, corridor access and automatic proximity-opening doors.
0.19.6 -> 0.19.7 : test first-person base traversal mode on V; captured mouse-look + WASD/Shift movement, outdoor/habitat/storage/corridor collision zones, automatic proximity sliding doors with first-person shell apertures, corridor/open-end traversal and floor-height tracking across terrain/interior decks/corridors.
0.19.7 -> 0.19.8 : FPV avatar scaled to corridor/door clearance with body-radius-aware corridor traversal; X11 relative mouse capture now follows window focus and releases the pointer immediately when the game loses focus.

0.20.2 - Corridor junction merge geometry rebuilt to carve host apertures and prevent overlapping corridor intersections.
0.20.2 -> 0.20.3 : 10x per-box carry/storage mass; Storage Dome capacity derived from usable interior volume; layer-major physical box stacks with actual package-height accumulation; dome packing constrained to a conservative cylinder fully inside the pressure hull.
0.20.3 -> 0.20.4 : corridor/structure access overhaul; unified structure floors and door thresholds with corridor deck level, removed corridor-colliding exterior stairs, tightened corridor-to-corridor and corridor-to-structure clearance, prevented later structure placement over corridors, and replaced broad FPV door-radius hull escapes with exact doorway/vestibule portal traversal.
0.20.4 -> 0.20.5 : FPV drop now resolves the clicked X/Z to the actual walkable floor height inside habitats, Storage Domes, corridors and corridor air-locks; corridor build snapping accepts any existing corridor segment/link/junction as a branch source; every exposed corridor endpoint now includes a collision-checked two-door pressure air-lock with interlocked FPV door rendering and exterior transition at the outer door.
0.20.5 -> 0.20.6 : corridor connection planner overhaul; reused habitat/storage entrances have no fixed branch limit, shared entrance fans are globally rebalanced, and corridor routing searches multiple smooth non-overlapping lanes around existing structures/corridors while explicit corridor targets remain merged shared junctions.
0.20.6 -> 0.20.7 : existing corridors are branchable at arbitrary centerline points, close structure entrances use compact non-overlapping merged connectors, corridor snap reach is expanded, and FPV spawn/floor tracking follows modeled structure basements, docking sleeves and authored stairs.
0.20.7 -> 0.20.8 : corridor interaction reset to node-first placement; any resolvable structure entrance can always be selected as a source regardless of the temporary sample direction, every visible corridor centerline point is prioritized as a source/destination intersection, terminal end snapping is limited to the actual end cap, and distinct points on the same host corridor can be targeted as separate junction nodes.

0.20.9
- Added click-drag resource-box selection pane when no placement tool is active.
- All ground resource packages projected inside the selection pane are selected together.
- Debug DEL can move a multi-selection of resource boxes into available Storage Domes.
- Corridor structure collision now follows actual projected mesh hull/foundation geometry instead of rectangular placement footprints.
- Added obstacle-search corridor routing with progressively wider A* detours around structures and unrelated corridors.
- Corridor routes remain clipped to the active playfield and preserve explicit corridor junction exceptions.
0.20.9 -> 0.21.0 : persistent named savegames; main-menu SAVE/LOAD workflow with text entry and save discovery; versioned atomic save format restores playfield, camera, colony status/time, seven-resource balances, habitats/resource structures, physical ground/storage boxes, construction progress/cost plans, corridor/supply/walkway topology and meshes, UI/debug/view settings, and display/fullscreen settings.
0.21.0 -> 0.21.1 : savegames are stored in a savegames/ directory beside the game executable, with current-working-directory fallback if the executable path cannot be resolved.
0.21.1 -> 0.21.2 : routing stress hardening across every supported playfield size (16..512); corridor fallback now samples multiple points/trunks, can reuse alternate Storage Dome service doors when a selected face is blocked, uses bounded one-bend detours, merges transversal corridor crossings into shared junction geometry, and avoids redundant all-pairs tubes; supply-channel routing is playfield-aware and reuses already-connected utility networks.
0.21.2 -> 0.21.3 : FPV pressure-volume overhaul; Storage Dome packages now rest on the dome's modeled floor, structure containment uses projected pressure-shell mesh geometry with body-radius clearance, structure floors follow modeled basement slabs and entrance stairs, and the FPV HUD explicitly distinguishes pressurized interiors/corridors/airlocks from exterior vacuum.
0.21.3 -> 0.22.0 : corridor placement interaction update; corridor branch previews are rendered at a reduced blueprint scale, explicit corridor-start branches can place valid end points again by fixing long-host-segment junction clearance, and runtime/menu/CLI semantic version reporting is unified through VERSION.
0.22.0 -> 0.22.1 : FPV traversal hardening; bidirectional mesh-level structure-shell containment, doorway-only entry/exit, complete generated docking-vestibule navigation, corridor-to-corridor pressure-volume continuity, diagonal doorway movement, and preserved modeled basement/stair floor tracking.
0.22.1 -> 0.22.2 : structural access hardening; exposed corridor ends are sealed bulkheads, ordinary structures and Storage Domes expose only completed pressure-docked entrances, POV placement is exterior-only, and the dedicated connected Air Lock is the sole exterior gateway into the pressurized corridor/structure network.
0.22.2 -> 0.23.0 : modular habitat/corridor architecture; all ten habitats split into outer and inner builders under the shared StructureModule access contract; explicit per-structure walkable deck heights drive POV and corridor docking stairs; mixed shell/glazing/foundation containment fixes Bio Dome/Cantine interior classification; corridor outer pressure shell and inner walk deck are instantiated through CorridorModule.
